    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Excellent! All tests are passing. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n### 1. Missing named export for `APPROVAL_STATUSES` in frai-core\n**File**: `packages/frai-core/src/finetune/index.js`\n\nThe test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only available in the default export. I added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` right after the imports.\n\n### 2. Incorrect `toxicityMetric` function signature\n**File**: `packages/frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js`\n\nThe `toxicityMetric` function had a different signature than the other metrics. When called from `runEvaluations`, it was receiving `(outputs, references)` but the second parameter was named `bannedTerms`, causing references to be treated as banned keywords. This resulted in false toxicity flags.\n\n**Fix**: Changed the signature from `toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references)` to match the pattern of other metrics, and now the function always uses the default banned terms (ignoring the references parameter which it doesn't need).\n\n## Test Results\n\u2705 All 28 tests in frai-core pass\n\u2705 All 11 tests in frai-gate pass  \n\u2705 All public exports remain functional",
